From a966aca4978c5c0795f5754e239d7c221edb0b91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: satelite-one release pin <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:01:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(release): pin the core to the frozen v0.1.6 revision

version.properties still pinned coreCommit=c35faabf4, which is the core the
0.5.10 release was cut from. That revision predates this round's ABI migration
and the uTLS hybrid-share pin, so a rebuild of the release tag would have
produced a different core than the one this round froze -- exactly the
non-reproducible-tag failure the pin exists to prevent.

c35faabf4 is 40 commits behind the frozen revision. Move the pin to the frozen
core commit and change nothing else: versionCode and versionName keep the
existing 0.5.10 release strategy, and no app tag is created here.

The release workflow resolves this value, fetches that exact commit from
Piggy-Cat-bit-shadow/sing-box, and builds libbox.aar from it, so the pin is
only effective once the frozen core commit is itself pushed to that
repository.
---
 version.properties | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/version.properties b/version.properties
index 4d9dc04..7fbb302 100644
--- a/version.properties
+++ b/version.properties
@@ -13,4 +13,4 @@ versionName=0.5.10
 # 开发用 CI(.github/workflows/android-ci.yml) 仍然跟随 testing HEAD。
 #
 # 发版前把这个值更新为要发布的内核 commit, 并与 app 一起提交。
-coreCommit=c35faabf402a4da93b8c31cdfad941b8b1528ffc
+coreCommit=0fbca85462689c1ea72f7f1af511540ff873aeba
-- 
2.54.0 (Apple Git-157)

